│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_shared_rotation_network                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses 24 distinct parameters across 26 gates, achieving a combined     │
│                          │ score of 0.60. The key bottleneck is the worst_group_margin_mean (0.35), indicating poor  │
│                          │ separation on difficult samples, despite good average accuracy.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Drawing inspiration from the context of the current ansatz, I observe:                    │
│                          │ 1. The current design separates pre/post rotations with fixed CZ couplings - this creates │
│                          │ rigid interaction patterns                                                                │
│                          │ 2. Parameter efficiency is critical: the score heavily penalizes redundant parameters     │
│                          │ 3. Robust separation requires capturing sample-specific difficulty with fewer degrees of  │
│                          │ freedom                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Novel approach:                                                                           │
│                          │ - **Aggressive parameter sharing**: Collapse per-qubit rotations into fewer shared        │
│                          │ parameters, reducing distinct params from 24 to ~8                                        │
│                          │ - **Adaptive interaction pattern**: Replace rigid linear CZ chain with alternating        │
│                          │ two-qubit parametrized gates (XX/YY/ZZ) that adapt to capture non-linear relationships    │
│                          │ - **Compact rotation structure**: Use only 2 shared RY parameters and 1 shared RZ         │
│                          │ parameter for rotation basis, repeated across all qubits                                  │
│                          │ - **Strategic two-qubit connectivity**: Apply parametrized gates on complementary qubit   │
│                          │ pairs to create richer entanglement patterns while maintaining efficiency                 │
│                          │ - **Depth optimization**: Reduce overall depth by consolidating operations and removing   │
│                          │ redundant post-rotations                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design trades off parameter count for richer, more adaptive interaction patterns     │
│                          │ that should improve worst-group margin through better feature extraction on hard samples. │
