│ patch_description        │ Replace the current architecture with a more parameter-efficient design that uses         │
│                          │ parametrized two-qubit gates (XX, YY, ZZ) with aggressive parameter sharing. The key      │
│                          │ insights are:                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Reduce single-qubit parameters through sharing**: Instead of 8 unique RY and 16      │
│                          │ unique RZ parameters, use only 2-3 shared rotation parameters that apply to multiple      │
│                          │ qubits based on structure (even/odd positions).                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Replace fixed CZ gates with parametrized XX/YY/ZZ gates**: These gates with shared   │
│                          │ parameters provide richer quantum interactions while maintaining parameter economy.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Add cross-diagonal entanglement**: Include non-linear chain connections (e.g., 0-2,  │
│                          │ 1-3, etc.) to increase connectivity and enable the model to learn correlations that       │
│                          │ generalize better to hard samples.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Strategic parameter sharing**: Use the same XX, YY, ZZ parameters across multiple    │
│                          │ gate applications within one block. This forces the model to learn patterns that work     │
│                          │ across different qubit pairs, improving generalization to unseen hard samples.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach targets the worst-group margin (0.35) by reducing overfitting to easy       │
│                          │ samples and forcing the model to learn more robust, symmetric decision boundaries that    │
│                          │ transfer to the hardest test samples.                                                     │
