│ patch_description        │ Analysis of the three programs:                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Seed program** (score: 0.60): 24 distinct parameters, good worst_group_margin        │
│                          │ (0.35), but low parameter_efficiency (0.04)                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Current program** (score: 0.64): Only 9 distinct parameters with aggressive          │
│                          │ parameter sharing (best efficiency: 0.09), slightly lower worst_group_margin (0.34) but   │
│                          │ better overall score                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Inspiration program** (score: 0.60): Same as seed - individual parameters per qubit  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program wins on parameter efficiency and overall score, but sacrifices some   │
│                          │ margin performance. The key insight is that parameter sharing dramatically improves       │
│                          │ efficiency without destroying performance.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Crossover strategy:**                                                                   │
│                          │ - Keep the current program's aggressive parameter sharing approach (RY fully shared, RZ   │
│                          │ pre/post paired by 2-qubit groups)                                                        │
│                          │ - Add back the full linear entanglement chain [0-1, 1-2, ..., 6-7] from the               │
│                          │ seed/inspiration programs (which is simpler and more proven)                              │
│                          │ - Remove the extra cross-qubit CZ gates [0-2, 1-3, 3-5, 4-6, 5-7] that add complexity     │
│                          │ without clear benefit                                                                     │
│                          │ - This hybrid approach maintains parameter economy while using the simpler, more robust   │
│                          │ entanglement pattern                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Maintain low parameter count (~9 distinct params)                                       │
│                          │ - Reduce depth/gate_count by removing redundant entanglement gates                        │
│                          │ - Potentially recover some worst_group_margin by using the proven linear entanglement     │
│                          │ pattern                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Better generalization through parameter economy                                         │
