│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_rx_shared_layer                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Add a shared RX rotation layer before the current RY rotations to enrich single-qubit     │
│                          │ expressivity with minimal overhead. This follows the successful pattern from the second   │
│                          │ program that achieved score 0.65, where aggressive parameter sharing improved both        │
│                          │ efficiency and worst_group_margin.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The RX layer uses a single shared parameter across all 8 qubits, adding only Δn_params=1  │
│                          │ while providing a complementary rotation axis to the existing RY+RZ structure. The        │
│                          │ RX-RY-RZ combination provides a more complete basis for single-qubit transformations,     │
│                          │ which should help the optimizer find better solutions for the hardest samples (improving  │
│                          │ worst_group_margin from 0.34 to potentially 0.35+).                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is consistent with the recommendation and the successful strategy in program 2 of    │
│                          │ maximizing parameter sharing to improve parameter_efficiency and generalization.          │
