│ patch_name               │ simplify_crz_entanglement                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current circuit has 108 gates with only 8 distinct parameters. While achieving        │
│                          │ perfect training accuracy, the worst_group_margin (0.35) suggests it may be overfitting   │
│                          │ to average samples rather than handling the hardest ones robustly.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Prior work (score 0.65) achieved similar results with only 81 gates by using aggressive   │
│                          │ parameter sharing with CRZ gates. I'll apply this lesson: replace the long-range ZZ       │
│                          │ entanglement block with shared-parameter CRZ gates and remove redundant mid-range RZ      │
│                          │ rotations. This reduces circuit complexity while maintaining expressivity through         │
│                          │ parameter sharing.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ 1. Remove the mid-range RZ layer (rz_mid appears redundant)                               │
│                          │ 2. Replace 5 long-range ZZ gates with 4 CRZ gates using a single shared parameter         │
│                          │ 3. Keep the essential nearest-neighbor and offset entanglement (XX, YY)                   │
│                          │ 4. Consolidate to 7 distinct parameters                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected benefit: Reduced gate count (from 108 to ~95), better generalization on hard     │
│                          │ samples, and improved robustness without sacrificing accuracy.                            │
