│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best elements from both programs to maximize robustness and   │
│                          │ parameter efficiency:                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the CRZ program (0.65 score)**: Uses the highly efficient CRZ parametrized      │
│                          │ gates with strategic parameter sharing. This achieves excellent accuracy with only 8      │
│                          │ distinct parameters and lower gate count (81), while maintaining strong                   │
│                          │ worst_group_margin (0.35).                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From the current program (0.65 score)**: The Ising gate structure (XX, YY, ZZ)       │
│                          │ provides superior validation_margin (0.73 vs 0.72) and perfect validation accuracy        │
│                          │ (1.00), indicating better generalization and harder-sample robustness.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Key improvements**:                                                                  │
│                          │    - Replace the expensive middle layers of XX/YY gates with targeted CRZ gates on key    │
│                          │ qubit pairs                                                                               │
│                          │    - Maintain the initial RY encoding layer but use selective parameter sharing like the  │
│                          │ CRZ program                                                                               │
│                          │    - Keep the long-range ZZ entanglement which contributes to validation_margin strength  │
│                          │    - Reduce depth from 24 to ~15-18 and gate_count from 108 to ~85                        │
│                          │    - Achieve the same 8 distinct parameters for maximum parameter efficiency              │
│                          │    - Improve convergence speed from 60 steps toward 90 (trading slightly longer training  │
│                          │ for better robustness)                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hybrid maintains the generalization quality of both approaches while reducing circuit │
│                          │ depth and gate overhead, which should improve the worst_group_margin through more stable  │
│                          │ parameter learning.                                                                       │
