│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parameterized_ising_entanglement                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses mostly single-qubit rotations with fixed two-qubit CRZ gates.   │
│                          │ Analysis of prior successful programs shows that:                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Parametrized Ising gates (XX, YY, ZZ) significantly outperformed fixed gates in the    │
│                          │ second prior program (score 0.65 vs baseline).                                            │
│                          │ 2. Strategic parameter sharing (even/odd qubits) combined with multiple entanglement      │
│                          │ layers improved worst_group_margin and generalization.                                    │
│                          │ 3. The recommendation to add RX rotations adds rotational diversity cheaply.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This new approach combines:                                                               │
│                          │ - **RX pre-layer** (shared across all qubits) for rotational diversity (+1 param)         │
│                          │ - **Parametrized Ising gates** instead of fixed CRZ, using strategic sharing to keep      │
│                          │ parameter count low                                                                       │
│                          │ - **Structured entanglement**: nearest-neighbor (XX), offset (YY), and long-range (ZZ)    │
│                          │ with different shared parameters                                                          │
│                          │ - **Post-entanglement rotations** (RY and RZ) for classical-to-quantum feature processing │
│                          │ - **Parameter economy**: Only 8-9 distinct parameters despite rich expressivity           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach should:                                                                     │
│                          │ - Improve worst_group_margin by richer entanglement patterns                              │
│                          │ - Maintain or reduce parameter count while increasing expressivity                        │
│                          │ - Accelerate convergence through better feature space mapping                             │
│                          │ - Better separate hard-to-classify samples through multi-scale entanglement               │
