│ patch_description        │ Replace the long-range ZZ gates in the third entangling block with CRZ gates using a      │
│                          │ shared parameter. This provides tunable phase control at each two-qubit interaction       │
│                          │ point, enabling better separation of hard samples. CRZ gates offer finer expressivity     │
│                          │ than ZZ for the same parameter count.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, reduce the rz_mid rotations to only even-indexed qubits (0, 2, 4, 6) to     │
│                          │ streamline the circuit, reducing gate count and potential overfitting while maintaining   │
│                          │ the symmetry pattern established in the initial layers.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These changes aim to improve worst_group_margin (currently stuck at 0.35) by giving the   │
│                          │ circuit more fine-grained control over entanglement, while slightly reducing overall      │
│                          │ complexity.                                                                               │
