                         Patch Metadata - Gen 17/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ cyclic_ising_mixer                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The prior programs achieved strong performance (0.65-0.66 combined score) with efficient  │
│                          │ parameter sharing and structured entanglement patterns. Key observations:                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The second program (score 0.66) outperformed the others by using only 7 distinct       │
│                          │ parameters and achieving faster convergence (30 steps vs 60-90), suggesting that          │
│                          │ aggressive parameter reuse is rewarded.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. The current program (score 0.65) has 8 distinct parameters and slower convergence (90  │
│                          │ steps), indicating over-parameterization despite good accuracy metrics.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. The worst_group_margin (0.35) is the bottleneck—we need stronger separation on hard    │
│                          │ samples without just adding parameters.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Novel approach: I'll combine the parameter efficiency of the best performer with a cyclic │
│                          │ ring topology (as suggested) using Ising gates instead of controlled rotations. Ising     │
│                          │ gates (XX, YY, ZZ) naturally create symmetric entanglement and are known to be efficient  │
│                          │ mixers in QAOA. The ring closure adds long-range connectivity at zero parameter cost.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Use a 3-layer structure: initial rotations → Ising entanglement rings → final rotations │
│                          │ - Aggressive parameter sharing: reuse the same few parameters across multiple gates       │
│                          │ - Employ alternating Ising types (XX, then YY) for richer correlation structure           │
│                          │ - Close the 8-qubit chain into a ring with a CZ gate on [7,0]                             │
│                          │ - Reduce distinct parameters to 4-5 for better generalization                             │
│                          │ - Replace CRZ with simpler XX/YY/ZZ for faster training convergence                       │
