│ patch_name               │ crz_adaptive_mid_layer                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.66) achieves good performance with 7 distinct parameters and │
│                          │ fast convergence (30 steps). However, there's room to improve worst_group_margin (0.35)   │
│                          │ which is critical for robust separation on hard samples.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Current program uses CRZ gates in the long-range block but lacks intermediate depth    │
│                          │ between first and third entangling blocks                                                 │
│                          │ 2. The "rz_mid" parameter from prior program (score 0.65) was removed, losing             │
│                          │ expressivity in the mid-layer                                                             │
│                          │ 3. Worst-group margin plateaus at 0.35—indicating the hard samples need better            │
│                          │ discrimination                                                                            │
│                          │ 4. Convergence is very fast (30 steps), suggesting the ansatz may be overfitting early    │
│                          │ rather than learning robust features                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ New strategy:                                                                             │
│                          │ - Restore selective RZ rotations between entangling blocks to deepen expressivity         │
│                          │ - Add a second long-range entangling layer (using CRZ on different qubit pairs) to create │
│                          │ cross-correlated phase relationships that help separate hard samples                      │
│                          │ - Introduce CRX instead of pure ZZ/CRZ for more flexible two-qubit control                │
│                          │ - Keep parameter count low (target ≤8 distinct) through aggressive sharing                │
│                          │ - Maintain the efficient XX/YY nearest-neighbor structure but supplement with             │
│                          │ strategically placed two-qubit phase gates                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This balances model capacity with parameter efficiency, aiming to push worst_group_margin │
│                          │ above 0.36 while keeping n_distinct_params ≤ 8.                                           │
