                         Patch Metadata - Gen 36/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dual_entanglement_motif                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The structural redesign implements a dual-repetition entanglement motif architecture that │
│                          │ replaces the ad-hoc mixing of different gate types with a systematic, reusable block      │
│                          │ structure. Instead of interleaving XX, YY, and CRZ gates in sequence, the new design      │
│                          │ explicitly constructs two identical entanglement blocks (XX → CRX → YY → CRZ), each       │
│                          │ reusing the same three entanglement parameters ("ent_nn", "ent_off", "ent_lr"). This      │
│                          │ achieves:                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Improved expressivity with parameter efficiency**: Doubling the proven               │
│                          │ seven-parameter substructure enriches representational power while keeping the distinct   │
│                          │ parameter count at 7, maintaining excellent parameter efficiency.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Structural clarity and modularity**: The repeating motif is immediately              │
│                          │ recognizable, making the architecture more maintainable and debuggable.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Consistent convergence profile**: Both prior programs converged in ~30 steps with    │
│                          │ zero generalization gap; the dual motif preserves this while targeting harder samples     │
│                          │ (worst_group_margin improvement).                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Enhanced hardest-sample discrimination**: The second entanglement block processes    │
│                          │ already-entangled qubits through the full motif again, allowing finer discrimination of   │
│                          │ difficult boundary cases without adding trainable parameters.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The architecture removes the fixed CZ layer (which added depth without parameters) and    │
│                          │ replaces it with a second parametrized entanglement motif, letting optimization tune both │
│                          │ blocks jointly for maximum separation on worst-case samples.                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0162                                                                                   │
