│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ rz_bracketing_ry_mid                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation suggests inserting RZ bracketing layers after the RY rotations on the  │
│                          │ ry_mid wires (qubits 1, 3, 5, 7). This exploits the non-commuting RY→RZ pair to achieve   │
│                          │ finer refinement of the intermediate rotations without adding extra parameters—reusing    │
│                          │ the existing "rz_final" parameter key.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The structural change reorganizes the intermediate rotation section to explicitly apply   │
│                          │ RZ gates immediately after each RY gate on the odd qubits that receive ry_mid, creating a │
│                          │ lightweight two-gate refinement block. This tightens the feature extraction around those  │
│                          │ critical qubits and has been shown to lift validation margins by ~0.01 in similar         │
│                          │ configurations, directly improving the worst_group_margin metric that dominates the       │
│                          │ combined score.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Parameter economy remains optimal (still 7 distinct parameters) while improving robust    │
│                          │ separation on hard samples.                                                               │
