                         Patch Metadata - Gen 39/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ decoupled_crx_hierarchy                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The prior programs achieved 0.67 combined score with 7 distinct parameters. The current   │
│                          │ program regressed to 0.66, likely due to the additional CRZ gate and the shift in CZ gate │
│                          │ patterns creating redundancy without improved expressivity.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insight: The recommendation to decouple CRX into a distinct "ent_crx" parameter was   │
│                          │ not yet explored. Currently, CRX gates either don't exist or share parameters with other  │
│                          │ layers. By introducing a dedicated narrow-angle CRX sublayer with its own parameter, we   │
│                          │ can:                                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Decouple rotation axes**: CRX (controlled X-rotation) operates fundamentally         │
│                          │ differently from XX/YY Ising gates and CRZ controlled rotations. Giving it a unique       │
│                          │ parameter allows the optimizer to learn independent amplitude scales.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Maintain parameter economy**: We stay at 7-8 distinct parameters (similar to winning │
│                          │ programs) while gaining fresh entanglement patterns.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Strategic placement**: Insert the CRX layer right after the first XX block to build  │
│                          │ asymmetric control-target relationships that complement the symmetric Ising gates.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Reduce gate bloat**: Remove the extra CRZ gate and revert to the more selective CZ   │
│                          │ pattern from the first winning program, reducing depth from 24 and gate count from 111.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The circuit hierarchy becomes:                                                            │
│                          │ - Initial RY (symmetry-breaking)                                                          │
│                          │ - XX nearest-neighbor (symmetric pair entanglement)                                       │
│                          │ - CRX offset (asymmetric controlled entanglement with dedicated parameter)                │
│                          │ - YY offset (complementary symmetric entanglement)                                        │
│                          │ - Intermediate RY (expressivity boost)                                                    │
│                          │ - Long-range CRZ (distance-2/3 control structures)                                        │
│                          │ - Fixed CZ skip-3 layer (hard-sample discrimination)                                      │
│                          │ - Final RZ (output rotation)                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design respects the winning structure while testing whether decoupling CRX unlocks   │
│                          │ better worst-group margins through more diverse entanglement patterns.                    │
