│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ cyclic_crx_closure                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current program scores 0.65 with a worst_group_margin of 0.34, which is the           │
│                          │ bottleneck limiting robust separation. Comparing to the prior generation (score 0.67,     │
│                          │ worst_group_margin 0.36), we see that the key loss came from:                             │
│                          │ 1. Increased n_distinct_params (8 vs 7) — parameter economy directly impacts scoring      │
│                          │ 2. Reduced worst_group_margin (0.34 vs 0.36) — harder samples are less well separated     │
│                          │ 3. Slower convergence (60 vs 30 steps) — training efficiency degraded                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation is to close the CRX sublayer into a cyclic pattern by adding a CRX     │
│                          │ gate from qubit 7 back to qubit 0, reusing the existing "ent_crx" parameter. This         │
│                          │ achieves:                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Connectivity improvement:** The three CRX gates currently form an open chain [1→2, 3→4, │
│                          │ 5→6]. Closing the loop [7→0] connects the boundary qubits and reinforces entanglement     │
│                          │ pathways across the full qubit ring, improving hard-sample discrimination                 │
│                          │ (worst_group_margin).                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Parameter efficiency:** Reusing "ent_crx" maintains n_distinct_params at 8 (no          │
│                          │ increase), but the shared gate pattern creates a more coherent entanglement structure     │
│                          │ that generalizes better from the small training set.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Analogy to prior success:** The prior generation used shared XX gates [0-1, 2-3, 4-5,   │
│                          │ 6-7] and shared YY gates [1-2, 3-4, 5-6]. This new CRX closure mirrors that proven        │
│                          │ ring-closure strategy, extending the internal connectivity without parameter              │
│                          │ proliferation.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The cyclic closure should tighten the qubit graph, improve separation on hard samples,    │
│                          │ and recover the robust margin performance lost in the current version.                    │
