╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ efficient_single_motif_crx                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of the three programs shows:                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Prior Program 1** (score 0.67): Compact single-motif design with 7 distinct params,  │
│                          │ 108 gates, depth 26, convergence at step 30. Uses a fixed CZ layer for hard-sample        │
│                          │ discrimination.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Prior Program 2** (score 0.67): Similar compact design with 7 distinct params, 105   │
│                          │ gates, depth 26, but adds RZ bracketing on odd qubits and removes some final RZ gates.    │
│                          │ Convergence at step 30.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Current Program** (score 0.66): Repeats the entire entanglement motif twice, leading │
│                          │ to bloat: 150 gates, depth 39, convergence at step 60. This redundancy hurts              │
│                          │ generalization and efficiency.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key observations:**                                                                     │
│                          │ - Both prior programs achieve 0.67 with economical single-motif designs                   │
│                          │ - The current doubled-motif approach degrades performance (0.66) despite having the same  │
│                          │ parameter count                                                                           │
│                          │ - Prior Program 1's fixed CZ layer + skip-3 pattern is effective for worst-group margin   │
│                          │ (0.36)                                                                                    │
│                          │ - Prior Program 2's CRX enrichment layer shows marginal improvement (105 vs 108 gates)    │
│                          │ with identical score                                                                      │
│                          │ - Convergence matters: single motif converges in 30 steps vs doubled motif in 60 steps    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Crossover strategy:**                                                                   │
│                          │ Combine the structural efficiency of Prior Program 1 (with fixed CZ discrimination layer) │
│                          │ with the CRX enrichment from Prior Program 2. This hybrid approach:                       │
│                          │ - Keeps single-motif simplicity (depth 26, gates ~108)                                    │
│                          │ - Adds CRX layer (proven to help without degrading score)                                 │
│                          │ - Includes fixed CZ for hard-sample discrimination                                        │
│                          │ - Maintains 7 distinct parameters for optimal parameter efficiency                        │
│                          │ - Expected convergence: ~30 steps                                                         │
