│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_crx_zz_backbone                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Reintroduce the CRX layer (which was present in the prior 0.67-score program) and add a   │
│                          │ complementary ZZ sublayer immediately after, both sharing the "ent_nn" parameter. This    │
│                          │ creates a richer XX→CRX→ZZ→YY entangling backbone that:                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Restores the CRX gates that contributed to the prior 0.67 score                        │
│                          │ 2. Adds Z-axis Ising interactions via ZZ gates to provide orthogonal expressivity         │
│                          │ 3. Keeps parameter count constant (7 distinct parameters) by parameter sharing            │
│                          │ 4. Improves worst_group_margin by enriching the circuit's ability to discriminate hard    │
│                          │ samples                                                                                   │
│                          │ 5. Maintains parameter efficiency while gaining expressivity                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The ZZ gates on pairs (0,1), (2,3), (4,5), (6,7) match the CRX spacing on offset pairs    │
│                          │ (1,2), (3,4), (5,6), creating complementary coverage.                                     │
