│                          │ 0.67, but enhance it with a ZZ layer as recommended. The current program is               │
│                          │ over-engineered with excessive depth (46 vs 23-26 in priors) and slower convergence (60   │
│                          │ vs 30 steps), hurting robustness.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ 1. Replace the dense ring-structure XX layer with the lean 4-pair nearest-neighbor XX     │
│                          │ 2. Use narrow CRX (3 gates, not 4) to bridge XX and YY                                    │
│                          │ 3. Add ZZ sublayer immediately after CRX, sharing "ent_nn" parameter for parameter        │
│                          │ economy                                                                                   │
│                          │ 4. Simplify final rotations (even qubits only) to reduce gate bloat                       │
│                          │ 5. Keep the long-range CRZ layer which provided good separation in prior versions         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces complexity while adding Z-axis Ising interactions, improving                 │
│                          │ expressivity-per-parameter and restoring fast convergence.                                │
