│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the inspiration program (score 0.67, 26 depth, 105 gates):**                    │
│                          │    - Uses selective final RZ rotations only on even qubits (0,2,4,6) instead of all 8     │
│                          │ qubits, which reduces parameter count and depth                                           │
│                          │    - Includes the RZ bracketing interleaved with intermediate RY on odd qubits, providing │
│                          │ better expressivity with controlled depth                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From the current program (score 0.66, 29 depth, 117 gates):**                        │
│                          │    - Retains the skip-3 CZ layer for hard-sample discrimination, which helped validation  │
│                          │ margin                                                                                    │
│                          │    - Keeps the 5-gate CRZ long-range entangling block (vs 4-gate variant)                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Key improvements:**                                                                  │
│                          │    - Removes the redundant CRX on (7,0) which was in the original seed but absent in top  │
│                          │ performers                                                                                │
│                          │    - Uses selective even-qubit RZ final layer (4 gates) instead of all 8 (8 gates) to     │
│                          │ reduce depth and gate count                                                               │
│                          │    - Keeps parametrized two-qubit gates for expressivity while maintaining parameter      │
│                          │ efficiency                                                                                │
│                          │    - Maintains 7 distinct parameters for strong generalization                            │
│                          │    - Expected to achieve faster convergence (closer to 30 steps vs 60) with improved      │
│                          │ worst_group_margin                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hybrid maintains the core validated entangling structure while reducing unnecessary   │
│                          │ depth and gate count, targeting the higher worst_group_margin (0.36) observed in the      │
│                          │ inspiration program.                                                                      │
