│ patch_name               │ zz_sandwich_crx_bridge                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Drawing inspiration from the prior programs' success with parameter sharing and           │
│                          │ multi-axis entanglement, this novel approach implements a "ZZ-sandwich" architecture that │
│                          │ strategically inserts parametrized ZZ gates between existing entanglement layers.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insights from context programs:                                                       │
│                          │ 1. The prior successes used 7 distinct parameters while achieving 0.67 combined score     │
│                          │ 2. Heavy reliance on nearest-neighbor and offset patterns suggests geometric locality     │
│                          │ matters                                                                                   │
│                          │ 3. The CRX bridge layer (from recommendation) can enrich entanglement without raising     │
│                          │ parameter count                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. Long-range CRZ gates help with hard-sample discrimination                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Novel approach:                                                                           │
│                          │ - Insert ZZ gates immediately after the CRX bridge to create an X-Z entanglement pair     │
│                          │ - Replace fixed CZ gates with parametrized alternatives where possible to improve         │
│                          │ gradient flow                                                                             │
│                          │ - Use aggressive parameter sharing (reuse "ent_nn" for multiple gate types) to maintain   │
│                          │ efficiency                                                                                │
│                          │ - Streamline the rotation layers to reduce depth while maintaining expressiveness         │
│                          │ - Focus on creating complementary entanglement patterns that bootstrap off each other     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The ZZ sandwich creates a coupled interaction pattern: XX→CRX→ZZ forms a complete basis   │
│                          │ coverage within a compact sublayer, improving robustness on hard samples without          │
│                          │ parameter bloat.                                                                          │
