│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_zz_after_crx_remove_cz                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program adds non-parametrized CZ gates that increase circuit depth/gate count │
│                          │ without contributing to parameter efficiency or improving worst_group_margin. Following   │
│                          │ the expert recommendation, we replace this with a targeted addition of shared-parameter   │
│                          │ ZZ gates immediately after the CRX layer. This:                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Removes the 5 fixed CZ gates (lines with CZ gates) that are depth-inefficient          │
│                          │ 2. Adds 4 ZZ gates on nearest-neighbor pairs (0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7) immediately after CRX   │
│                          │ 3. Reuses the existing "ent_nn" parameter, keeping n_distinct_params at 7                 │
│                          │ 4. Provides Z-axis Ising interactions to complement the X-axis interactions from XX and   │
│                          │ CRX                                                                                       │
│                          │ 5. Should improve worst_group_margin by enriching feature space for hard samples          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The ZZ gates on the same qubit pairs as earlier XX gates create a richer entanglement     │
│                          │ pattern without parameter inflation.                                                      │
