│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ optimized_crossover_ansatz                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best elements from three candidates:                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From Prior Program 1 (baseline with CZ layer)**: The skip-3 CZ entangling layer      │
│                          │ provides hard-sample discrimination with fixed gates (no extra parameters), which helped  │
│                          │ achieve worst_group_margin_mean of 0.36.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From Current Program (cyclic CRX bridge)**: The cyclic CRX bridge layer with wires   │
│                          │ [7,0] creates wraparound entanglement, reducing depth from 26 to 23 while maintaining     │
│                          │ performance. This is more efficient than adding standalone CRX gates.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **From Prior Program 2 (selective final RZ)**: Applies RZ only to even qubits          │
│                          │ [0,2,4,6] rather than all 8 qubits. This reduces gate count and parameters while          │
│                          │ maintaining performance (validation accuracy stayed at 1.00).                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Intermediate RZ bracketing on odd qubits**: After ry_mid, adding selective RZ gates  │
│                          │ on odd qubits [1,3,5,7] (inspired by Prior Program 2) provides additional expressiveness  │
│                          │ for hard samples without increasing the distinct parameter count (reusing rz_final).      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that:                                                                  │
│                          │ - The CZ skip-3 layer (fixed gates) provides discrimination without parameter cost        │
│                          │ - The cyclic CRX bridge is more efficient than standalone gates                           │
│                          │ - Selective application of final rotations (only even qubits) reduces overhead            │
│                          │ - Strategic RZ placement on odd qubits enriches expressiveness for worst-case samples     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This combination should achieve:                                                          │
│                          │ - Better worst_group_margin (from CZ layer + strategic RZ placement)                      │
│                          │ - Lower depth and gate count (from cyclic CRX and selective RZ)                           │
│                          │ - Same parameter efficiency (7 distinct params, 9 total params)                           │
│                          │ - Improved robustness to hard samples through targeted middle-layer bracketing            │
