                         Patch Metadata - Gen 57/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ reduce_final_rz_to_even_qubits                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current design applies RZ to all 8 qubits in the final layer with full parameter      │
│                          │ sharing (all use "rz_final"). This is parameter-efficient but creates                     │
│                          │ over-parameterization on odd qubits which already receive rich rotations (RY in initial   │
│                          │ layer + RY in intermediate + bracketing).                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By reducing the final RZ layer to only even-indexed qubits (0, 2, 4, 6), we:              │
│                          │ 1. Drop from 6 to 5 distinct parameters, improving parameter efficiency further           │
│                          │ 2. Maintain expressivity since odd qubits still have sufficient rotation degrees of       │
│                          │ freedom earlier in the circuit                                                            │
│                          │ 3. Reduce circuit depth and gate count, improving computational efficiency                │
│                          │ 4. Force the optimizer to rely more on earlier entangling blocks to discriminate samples, │
│                          │ potentially improving worst-group margin through better distributed feature learning      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This aligns with the principle that fewer, well-placed parameters with stronger           │
│                          │ individual impact generalize better than many redundant ones.                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0107                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 0; deleted: 4; modified: 1;                                                        │
