│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ swap_yy_to_crx_offset_block                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the offset nearest-neighbor YY gates in the second entangling block with CRX      │
│                          │ gates using the same shared parameter "ent_nn". This architectural diversification is     │
│                          │ inspired by Gen 48's 0.66→0.67 improvement when CRX enriched the entanglement space.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Rationale:                                                                                │
│                          │ - YY gates and CRX gates operate on different quantum principles (symmetric interaction   │
│                          │ vs controlled rotation)                                                                   │
│                          │ - The current approach stacks XX + CRX + YY on the same parameter, creating potential     │
│                          │ redundancy                                                                                │
│                          │ - Replacing YY with CRX should improve robustness on the hardest samples                  │
│                          │ (worst_group_margin_mean)                                                                 │
│                          │ - Maintains parameter economy (still 6 distinct parameters)                               │
│                          │ - Reduces total gate count from 102 to 96, improving parameter efficiency metric          │
│                          │ - The recommended edit directly targets the bottleneck of worst-case separation           │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0106                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
