│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ deepen_with_param_sharing                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ This edit combines two improvements:                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Reduce parameter count from 6 to 5 distinct parameters**: Merge the initial rotation │
│                          │ parameters `ry_even` and `ry_odd` into a single `ry` parameter. This extreme parameter    │
│                          │ sharing has proven effective (program 2 scored 0.69) and improves parameter efficiency,   │
│                          │ which is a primary scoring factor.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Deepen circuit expressivity**: Insert a second XX–CRX–YY entanglement block after    │
│                          │ the existing blocks. This reuses the `ent_nn` parameter (no new parameters) but increases │
│                          │ gate count and depth, which should improve the worst_group_margin_mean (currently 0.36,   │
│                          │ the main bottleneck). The deeper circuit allows the model to separate harder samples more │
│                          │ effectively.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The rationale: Robust separation on the hardest samples (worst_group_margin) is the       │
│                          │ limiting factor. By combining minimal parameter overhead (actually reducing params) with  │
│                          │ increased expressivity through an additional entanglement sequence, we can improve both   │
│                          │ parameter efficiency and worst-group performance.                                         │
