│ patch_name               │ unify_params_to_four                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The best prior program achieved 0.69 with only 5 distinct parameters through aggressive   │
│                          │ parameter sharing. The current program regressed to 6 distinct parameters by splitting    │
│                          │ initial RY into ry_even/ry_odd and keeping ent_lr separate from ent_nn.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit unifies parameters back to 4 distinct ones:                                     │
│                          │ 1. Merge ry_even and ry_odd → ry (single shared parameter for all initial rotations)      │
│                          │ 2. Merge ent_lr → ent_nn (all entanglers share one parameter, as recommended)             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces the parameter count from 6 to 4 distinct parameters while preserving the     │
│                          │ streamlined gate structure. Parameter economy is the primary differentiator per the       │
│                          │ scoring rules - fewer distinct parameters ALWAYS scores higher with no diminishing        │
│                          │ returns. The recommendation explicitly suggests this unification to probe the             │
│                          │ expressivity threshold that gave 0.69 with 5 parameters.                                  │
